    <DataNode elementId="AT1G76150-MONOMER" textLabel="enoyl-CoA hydratase 2" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q8VYI3" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="335" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">AT1G76150 encodes a monofunctional enoyl-CoA hydratase 2. In-vitro enzyme assays demonstrated that the Arabidopsis enoyl-CoA hydratase 2 catalyzed the reversible conversion of trans-2-enoyl-CoA to 3R-hydroxyacyl-CoA. Overexpression and underexpression followed by metabolic profiling indicated that in vivo the enzyme is involved in degradation of fatty acids with a cis-unsaturated double bond at an even-number carbon |CITS: [16982622]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G76150-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G76150.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q8VYI3" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="enoyl-CoA hydratase II" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-10752" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0005777" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT1G76150.1" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":AMBIGUOUS" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT1G76150" />
      <Property key="^citations" value="16982622" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-PEROXISOME-PL" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_16982622" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT1G65520-MONOMER" textLabel="Enoyl-CoA delta isomerase 1, peroxisomal" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O04469" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">There are three genes in the Arabidopsis genome encoding delta3-delta2-enoyl-CoA isomerase. Functional complementation experiment of a yeast mutant indicated all three genes are functional. In vitro enzyme assay also confirmed activity of ECI2 and ECI3. However, unlike ECI1 and ECI2 which are located in the peroxisome, ECI3 is located in the cytosol, not a location where fatty acid degradation occurs. It was speculated that ECI3 may still function in the cis/trans isomerization of similar double bonds of cytosolic metabolites.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G65520-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G65520.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="O04469" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="Delta(3),Delta(2)-enoyl CoA isomerase 1" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="AtECI1" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33196, RXN-10753" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT1G65520.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT1G65520" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_18657232" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT4G14430-MONOMER" textLabel="Enoyl-CoA delta isomerase 2, peroxisomal" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O23299" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">ECI2 along with two other genes (ECI1, ECI3) in the Arabidopsis genome encode delta3-delta2-enoyl-CoA isomerases |CITS:[18657232]|. Functional complementation experiments using a yeast mutant indicate that all three genes are functional. In vitro enzyme assays confirm the activity of ECI2 and ECI3. ECI1 and ECI2 are located in the peroxisome |CITS:[17951448]|. The gene encoding this enzyme was also identified in a screen for indole-3-butyric acid (IBA)-resistant mutants |CITS:[18725356]| and called IBR3. This enzyme is predicted to catalyze a step in a &amp;beta;-oxidation-like conversion of the IBA storage compound to the biologically active auxin, indole-3-acetic acid (IAA) |CITS:[18725356]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G14430-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT4G14430.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="O23299" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="Delta(3),Delta(2)-enoyl CoA isomerase 2" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="AtECI2" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="Indole-3-butyric acid response 10" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33410, RXN-10754" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT4G14430.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT4G14430" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_18657232" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_17951448" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_18725356" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT4G14440-MONOMER" textLabel="Enoyl-CoA delta isomerase 3" type="Protein">
